    "title": "KoalaBear m2 r4 coordinate negative loop-budget gate",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "at most two antipodal common-K edge orbits in negative parity and a five-skeleton exact remainder",
    "statement": "Every antipodal common-K J-edge makes q=0 and hence forces a root of the degree-at-most-two form A_1. Three loop fibers would force A_1=0, contradicting the nonzero q equation at a required nonloop edge. Therefore negative parity has at most two K loops. The seven injective pair-multiplicity skeletons reduce exactly to five, and one or two loops pin the corresponding factors of A_1. The five survivors and the coordinate orientation remain open.",
